	(text "BAND_A -> K1/K4, BAND_B -> K2/K5, BAND_C -> K3/K6.\nQ6 (BAND_A): 2 coils, 42 mA nom (5 V / 237 R),\n  <= 49 mA at 5.25 V, -10 % coil R.\nQ7 (BAND_B), Q9 (BAND_C): 2 coils each, 42 mA nom, <= 49 mA.\nAO3400A: 5.7 A cont., 48 mR @ Vgs 2.5 V -> <5 mV drop.\nOne 1N4148W flyback per coil, at each relay."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 184.15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.0 1.0)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "52c2fe21-26fa-40ea-9a04-476c884977b0")
	)
	(text "Band code (BAND_A, BAND_B, BAND_C):\n 0 0 0  80/60 m    (all relays off, NC path, default)\n 0 1 0  40/30 m    (K2, K5 on)\n 1 0 0  20/17 m    (K1, K4 on)\n 1 0 1  15/12/10 m (K1, K4, K3, K6 on)\nOther codes unused; never more than 4 coils on.\nUnselected filters float (open at both ends).\n+5V relay load: 0 / 42 / 42 / 84 mA nominal (<=98 mA worst).\nRelay pins: COM right, NC lower left, NO upper left; pole 2 unused.\nInput and output paths never share a relay body.\nLayout: keep K1-K2-K3 and K4-K5-K6 traces short,\n  50 ohm CPWG over solid GND, filters next to their relays."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 113.03 157.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.0 1.0)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bf48fcd4-b38f-4dd8-8490-463212c575b3")
	)
